  "hook": "Nina Ackermann and Calloway Hayes started at Keller Crane LLP on the same Monday in September. They were both Stanford Law. They were both gunning for the M&A partner slot that would open in eighteen months. They were both too smart to be friends. For the first seventeen months, they billed past each other, beat each other to partner's doors, and swapped deals in the same breath with the same clients. In month eighteen, the firm's biggest client demanded they work the same deal. Six weeks in a conference room. One bathroom. Neither of them slept.",
